    ('open_meteo_promotion_clearance', 'Open-Meteo promotion clearance', 'pass', 'The complete authenticated Gmail record was checked read-only on 2026-08-29. The 06:05:07 +05:00 request described Nimbo as free and non-monetized, with no subscriptions, advertising, paid features, affiliate links, accounts, analytics SDK, or sale of user data, and limited promotion to unpaid localized posts, one personalized contact plus at most one follow-up, genuine Apple/Google editorial submissions, and ordinary unpaid links. At 17:25 +05:00, Nicoletta Addimando via OpenMeteo GmbH replied in ticket 234272 and explicitly confirmed that under those terms Nimbo is entitled to use the non-commercial API. This pass is limited to that exact scope and the published Free API limits; monetization, paid promotion, attribution removal, limit changes, or other material facts require a new licensing decision.', 'Preserve the confirmed scope and reopen licensing review before any material monetization, promotion, attribution, endpoint, or usage-limit change'),
    ('release_artifact_source_sync', 'Release artifact source sync', 'blocked', 'Product/build-input commit 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652 resolves to Android phone 1.1.0 (8), Wear OS 1.1.0 (1000008), and Apple 1.1.0 (6). Exact-source GitHub Actions run 33300967788 passed the ordinary Android/iOS jobs, all 15 Compose UI tests across the API 24 phone, API 36 phone, and API 36 tablet profiles, and all 18 Apple surface-state tests. The protected release-signing environment now contains all 8/8 required secrets. Candidate run 33368227872 stopped at Apple export because a manual signing style was incompatible with Xcode-managed profiles. Run 33375162729 signed the Android phone and Wear bundles and completed Apple archive export, but the fail-closed byte verifier rejected the exported and retained app/widget because Xcode omitted their required App Group entitlement; cleanup succeeded and signed-candidate upload was skipped. The repository now contains an unproven hosted correction that restores only the App Group authorized by the protected profiles and requires exact ExportOptions, protected-profile UUID/name/SHA, workflow, and verifier provenance. Until a new hosted run passes, no signed package or schema-v3 receipt exists, 0/3 current artifacts are byte-verified, and the manifest remains blocked.', 'Run the hardened master-only hosted workflow, independently verify and retain its receipt and bytes, then bind exact physical QA to those retained artifacts'),
